CAT = "cpaaudEvidence"; SEG = "EVD"
Q = [
("Which source of evidence is generally the most reliable?",
 "Sent directly by a third party", ["Generated inside the entity", "Given orally by management", "A photocopy supplied by the client"],
 "Evidence from independent outside sources, obtained directly by the auditor, is more reliable than internal, oral or copied evidence."),
("The appropriateness of audit evidence is a measure of its:",
 "Relevance and reliability", ["Quantity and cost to obtain", "Timing and extent of testing", "Source and volume of documents"],
 "Sufficiency is the quantity of evidence. Appropriateness is its quality, meaning relevance and reliability."),
("Vouching recorded sales entries back to shipping documents mainly tests:",
 "Occurrence", ["Completeness", "Cutoff only", "Classification"],
 "Starting from the records and going to the source documents tests whether recorded transactions actually happened."),
("Tracing shipping documents forward to recorded sales mainly tests:",
 "Completeness", ["Occurrence", "Rights and obligations", "Presentation"],
 "Starting from the source documents and going to the records tests whether every real transaction was recorded."),
("A search for unrecorded liabilities is best performed by examining:",
 "Payments made after year-end", ["Year-end trial balance totals", "Prior year's payables list", "Open purchase orders only"],
 "Cash disbursements after the balance sheet date, and unpaid invoices received then, show liabilities that existed at year-end but were not recorded."),
("In an audit of a nonissuer, negative confirmations of receivables are suitable as the only substantive procedure only when, among other conditions:",
 "A low exception rate is expected", ["Balances are few and large", "Control risk is assessed high", "Customers are likely to ignore them"],
 "Negative confirmations alone are used when the risk of material misstatement is low, the population has many small homogeneous balances, few exceptions are expected and recipients are not expected to disregard them."),
("A customer does not reply to a positive confirmation request. The best alternative procedure is to examine:",
 "Cash received after year-end", ["The customer's credit file", "The aged trial balance", "The client's sales budget"],
 "Subsequent cash receipts matched to the specific invoices that made up the year-end balance give strong evidence of existence."),
("When sending confirmations, the auditor should:",
 "Keep control of the requests", ["Let the client mail them", "Ask replies to go to the client", "Send only to related parties"],
 "The auditor maintains control over confirmation requests and responses to reduce the risk of interception or alteration."),
("Under AU-C 520, when are analytical procedures required in an audit of a nonissuer?",
 "Near the end of the audit", ["Only as substantive tests", "Only for revenue", "Only when controls fail"],
 "Analytical procedures are required in risk assessment and near the end of the audit to form an overall conclusion. Substantive analytics are optional."),
("For a substantive analytical procedure, which expectation is most precise?",
 "Monthly figures by store", ["Annual company-wide totals", "Published industry averages", "Last year's audited balance"],
 "More disaggregated data, such as monthly amounts by location, give a more precise expectation that can detect smaller misstatements."),
("An auditor recomputes interest expense by multiplying average debt by the stated rate. This is:",
 "A substantive analytical procedure", ["A test of operating controls", "A walkthrough of the interest process", "An external confirmation"],
 "Building an expectation from relationships among data, here debt and rates, and comparing it with the recorded amount is a substantive analytical procedure."),
("The bank cutoff statement obtained shortly after year-end is mainly used to verify:",
 "Reconciling items on the bank rec", ["Interest rates on bank loans", "Next year's cash budget", "The client's credit rating"],
 "The auditor uses it to check that deposits in transit cleared and that outstanding checks cleared for the right amounts."),
("Check kiting is most likely detected by preparing a:",
 "Schedule of interbank transfers", ["Receivables aging schedule", "Review of the payroll register totals", "Fixed asset rollforward"],
 "A bank transfer schedule compares the dates transfers were recorded in the books and cleared each bank, revealing cash counted in two accounts."),
("Reperforming a client's year-end receivables aging using audit software mainly tests:",
 "Accuracy of the aging", ["Existence of customers", "Rights to receivables", "Occurrence of sales"],
 "Reperformance shows whether the client sorted balances correctly by age, which supports the allowance computation."),
("Before relying on a client-generated report in a substantive test, the auditor should test the report's:",
 "Completeness and accuracy", ["Format and presentation", "Approval date and signature", "Distribution list and users"],
 "Information produced by the entity is evidence only if the auditor tests, or tests controls over, its completeness and accuracy and the precision of the data."),
("An auditor uses data analytics to compare every sales invoice with shipping data. Compared with sampling, this approach:",
 "Tests the whole population", ["Removes all audit risk", "Replaces all inquiry", "Requires no data checks"],
 "Data analytics can test 100% of a population for a defined attribute, but the auditor must still validate the data and follow up exceptions."),
("Inquiry of management alone is:",
 "Not sufficient by itself", ["Enough for a significant risk", "The most reliable evidence", "Enough for controls testing"],
 "Inquiry alone does not give sufficient appropriate evidence to detect a material misstatement or test the operating effectiveness of controls."),
("To test the operating effectiveness of a control that leaves no documentary trail, the auditor would most likely use:",
 "Observation and inquiry", ["External confirmation", "Recalculation of totals", "Vouching to documents"],
 "When a control leaves no document behind, such as segregation of duties, the auditor observes it being performed and corroborates by inquiry."),
("Testing controls at an interim date, the auditor should then obtain evidence for:",
 "The remaining period", ["Only the prior year", "Year-end balances only", "The next fiscal year"],
 "Evidence about operating effectiveness at an interim date needs further evidence about changes in, and operation of, controls in the remaining period to year-end."),
("Observing a client's physical inventory count mainly tests:",
 "Existence", ["Valuation", "Rights and obligations", "Classification"],
 "Observing the count and making test counts gives evidence that recorded inventory exists. Valuation needs price tests and obsolescence review."),
("A recalculation of depreciation expense from the fixed asset register provides evidence about:",
 "Accuracy and valuation", ["Existence of assets", "Rights to the assets", "Occurrence of purchases"],
 "Recomputing depreciation tests that the expense and accumulated depreciation are mathematically correct, supporting accuracy and valuation."),
("Examining a deed and property tax bills gives evidence that a building:",
 "Is owned by the entity", ["Is carried at fair value", "Was recorded in the right year", "Is fully insured against loss"],
 "Title documents and tax bills in the entity's name support the rights and obligations assertion."),
("Under PCAOB AS 2310, the auditor should perform confirmation procedures for:",
 "Cash held by third parties", ["Every expense account", "Accrued payroll balances", "Retained earnings"],
 "AS 2310, adopted in 2023 and effective for fiscal years ending on or after June 15, 2025, requires confirming cash and cash equivalents held by third parties and accounts receivable, unless an exception applies."),
("Evidence that is gathered to test an assertion should be most persuasive when:",
 "The assessed risk is higher", ["The account is immaterial", "Controls are strong", "The client is a nonissuer"],
 "The higher the assessed risk of material misstatement, the more persuasive the evidence the auditor needs."),
]
